traffic.</p></abstract><kwd-group xml:lang="en"><title>Keywords</title><kwd>Asian Elephants</kwd><kwd>behavioural plasticity</kwd><kwd>conservation</kwd><kwd>Elephant cognition</kwd><kwd>Elephants’ food solicitation</kwd><kwd>ethology</kwd><kwd>road ecology</kwd><kwd>Sri Lanka</kwd><kwd>wildlife-human negative interaction</kwd></kwd-group><counts><page-count count="5"/></counts><custom-meta-group><custom-meta><meta-name>issue-cover</meta-name><meta-value><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://threatenedtaxa.org/public/journals/1/cover_issue_356_en.jpg"/></meta-value></custom-meta></custom-meta-group><custom-meta-group/></article-meta></front><body/></article>			</metadata>
